# {{.Name}}

A grist application, scaffolded by `grist new {{.Name}}`: items added to
a store that holds at most five of each (`add-item`, refused `invalid`,
and `full` by the `capacity` rule, which guards every addition), shown (`show-item`), tallied after each addition (the
`tally` processor) and sent to a warehouse (the `shelve` processor,
calling `Receive` of the declared dependency `Warehouse`: in a
simulation, its default double, lossy). It is checked against its Quint model with nothing
annotated: grist records every block's step, and the model's skeleton
and both bindings are generated from the App's catalog.

| file | what it is |
|---|---|
| [app.go](app.go), [commands.go](commands.go), [rules.go](rules.go), [queries.go](queries.go), [processors.go](processors.go), [deps.go](deps.go) | the events, the read model (`stock`, keyed by item), the command, the rule (`capacity`, on `item-added`: `grist.NewRule`), the query, the processors, the warehouse (a dependency and its call) |
| [model/{{.Name}}_rules.qnt](model/{{.Name}}_rules.qnt) | written by hand: the rules the skeleton calls (each command's outcome, events and the reads it needs, the rule's verdict and its reads, the query's answer, the processors' events, the warehouse's request) |
| [model/{{.Name}}.qnt](model/{{.Name}}.qnt) | written by hand: the invariants, each marked for its binding (`// grist: invariant`); the modules the bindings name |
| [model/{{.Name}}_gen.qnt](model/{{.Name}}_gen.qnt) (the events), [model/{{.Name}}_steps.qnt](model/{{.Name}}_steps.qnt) (the actions), `*.binding.yaml`, [model/grist.qnt](model/grist.qnt) | generated: `go run ./cmd/{{.Name}} model` (never edit them; `TestGenerated` fails when they are stale) |
| [cmd/{{.Name}}](cmd/{{.Name}}/main.go) | the binary (`grist.Main`): `model`, `catalog`, `verify`, `serve -db sqlite:PATH` |
| [testdata/mutants](testdata/mutants) | `noInvalid`: the quantity check left out; `drop-capacity` is generated (`gristtest.RuleMutants(App)`: the app with its rule dropped); `qtest.Mutants` finds and runs them all |

## Which check catches which mutant

| test | configuration | catches |
|---|---|---|
| `TestFaithful` | one tenant, three clients, commit faults, node crashes, a lossy API and warehouse | nothing: `Conforms`, `All(Settles)`, commit faults reached, every block of the catalog taken (`gristtest.Catalog(App).Exercised()`) |
| `TestFaithfulAtClients` | the same runs at the clients, linearized | nothing: `Conforms` |
| `TestMutant` (`noInvalid`) | `TestFaithful`'s workload, no faults | `Some(Rejects("addItem"))`: an addition of none or fewer commits where the model refuses it (`TestFaithful` is the contrast) |
| `TestScenariosPossible` | the model on its own (`qtest.Possible`) | a model too strict for the `fill up` scenario (an item filled, an addition past its capacity refused `full`) to happen |
| `TestFull` | two clients filling one item, no faults | nothing: `None(Rejects("addItem"))` (`drop-capacity`'s contrast), some run following the `fill up` scenario (`gristtest.Scenario`) |
| `TestMutant` (`drop-capacity`, generated) | the same, the `capacity` rule dropped | `gristtest.DroppedRule`'s claim, `Some(Rejects("addItem"))`: an addition past the capacity commits where the generated guard (`capacityRefusal`) refuses it |
| `TestRealHTTP` | the real tier: SQLite, real HTTP, the warehouse's default double in process, every fifth answer lost (gristtest.Tier) | nothing: both bindings conform, every answer has its store-side step |
| `TestGenerated` | the generated files against the catalog | a block changed without regenerating |

## Next

Add a block (an event, a command, a rule, a processor, a dependency's call) in Go, regenerate (`go
run ./cmd/{{.Name}} model`: it names each new hole and a stub for it),
fill the holes in `model/{{.Name}}_rules.qnt`, mark the invariants in
`model/{{.Name}}.qnt`, and write a
mutant per claim. [grist's user guide](https://github.com/chucklehead-dev/gotogether/blob/main/docs/grist-guide.md)
says how, block by block (the `grist` skill, for an agent).

```sh
go test -short -v ./...        # every claim, each test's summary (needs quint on PATH; about a minute)
go test ./...                  # and Hegel's shrinks (about 6 minutes)
./run-demo.sh
MUTANT=noInvalid ./run-demo.sh
MUTANT=drop-capacity ./run-demo.sh
```
